WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.084
- Yo, D, what up?

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:02.585
- Yo, Melo, what's up, man?

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.046
- You ever seen a female quarterback in Hawaii?

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.425
- She's the starting quarterback for that high school in Honolulu, right?

00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:10.593
- She's legit. And she's got a cannon.

00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:11.681
I'mma send you the details

00:00:11.681 --> 00:00:13.104
and let you know. I'll keep you posted.

00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:14.102
- Yeah, man, I'm game.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:14.914
- Let's do this.

00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:47.692
- High school football in Hawaii—sounds nice.

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:51.760
But for Alexandria Buchanan, it's not just another day in paradise.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.124
Last season, she earned the title of only

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.702
female starting varsity QB in Hawaii.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.517
No wonder she went viral.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:04.264
She breaks her team's four-year losing streak, and now she's fighting for her job.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:11.780
- Football is a male-dominant sport. Everybody knows that. 

00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:15.670
- She's, um, fought for everything that she's earned. Nothing's been given to her. 

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:19.023
- People always say, like, especially in comments

00:01:19.023 --> 00:01:21.681
on articles or whatever, like, "People aren't gonna hit her,"

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.605
"They're gonna look like the bad guy, cuz it's a girl,"

00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:25.185
like, "They're just gonna let her go."

00:01:25.813 --> 00:01:27.982
In the stands, people are saying things

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:33.551
like, "Get her out," or "Get the other guy in" or "Why is she starting?"

00:01:35.348 --> 00:01:41.145
Football is a contact sport. I'm expecting to get hit. I'm not in flag football anymore.

00:01:45.588 --> 00:01:49.843
You can't say that just because I'm a girl people will take it lightly.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.656
And it's just frustrating because I get hit. [Laughing]

00:01:54.648 --> 00:01:55.504
I get hit a lot

00:01:56.344 --> 00:01:58.033
and I can take it.

00:02:13.623 --> 00:02:18.211
- Throwing has always been fun for me. That's what I really enjoy doing. 

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.357
Nice.

00:02:20.424 --> 00:02:21.299
Ooh. Good catch!

00:02:22.259 --> 00:02:27.556
It's hard for people to understand, like, a girl taking that position. 

00:02:27.984 --> 00:02:28.984
Hut, hut.

00:02:29.454 --> 00:02:33.792
I know I work hard, and football is something I'm really passionate about. 

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.172
You have to remember to do your job.

00:02:39.377 --> 00:02:43.465
And I don't want people to think just because I'm a girl they have to stop doing that.

00:02:47.769 --> 00:02:56.236
♪♪♪ Eager eyes are watching, hearts are beating fast.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:04.157
For McKinley's honor, FIGHT, team, to the last. ♪♪♪

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.201
- Well, I think it's always been about the team.

00:03:09.779 --> 00:03:12.319
I want to make sure these kids understand that, you know?

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:16.960
I mean, not one person can carry the team in a game situation.

00:03:17.811 --> 00:03:21.356
- No matter how bad or good I'm doing, they've stuck it out with me.

00:03:22.712 --> 00:03:25.556
- I love how we can look at each other as actual brothers and sisters.

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:28.927
- We're all, like, close to each other. We don't really bring anyone down. 

00:03:30.582 --> 00:03:35.315
- I really feel like they're my second family. That's just how a team should always be.

00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:44.080
My first game, I just went in for a couple plays, and I got hit. 

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.693
And I got up, and I was like, "Oh, that's not too bad. Like, I can handle this."

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:55.067
That first play went fine. All the other plays went fine.

00:03:55.061 --> 00:03:58.458
And then after that I just started building up confidence that I needed.

00:03:58.535 --> 00:03:59.536
[Cheering]

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.359
That's when they put me at starting, like, for the JV team.

00:04:04.716 --> 00:04:09.095
I was completing my passes, I was making the right reads for the most part. 

00:04:09.251 --> 00:04:10.378
- And she came back one day, and

00:04:10.372 --> 00:04:12.862
she said, "My coach wants to talk to you." [Laughing] That's what she said.

00:04:13.745 --> 00:04:16.520
He's like, "You know, Mr. Buchanan," he said.  "you know your daughter 

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.261
has something that I don't think anybody even understands yet.

00:04:20.662 --> 00:04:23.373
I want her to come on the varsity football team."

00:04:23.831 --> 00:04:27.042
- For me, it really doesn't matter. I think if you have a passion

00:04:27.038 --> 00:04:29.641
to want to do something, then good for you.

00:04:29.965 --> 00:04:34.302
More so if you're a female playing a male-dominant sport, right?

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.677
- She took the field. Everybody erupted. 

00:04:37.947 --> 00:04:40.603
And, you know, a few plays later, she made history. 

00:04:41.031 --> 00:04:43.868
- History was made as McKinley's Alexandria Buchanan

00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:46.809
became the first-ever female to start at quarterback in a

00:04:46.806 --> 00:04:50.992
Hawaii varsity football game, tossing the first female touchdown ever. 

00:04:50.991 --> 00:04:53.602
South Pacific Bureau, let's hear it for Alexandria.

00:04:54.055 --> 00:04:56.433
- That prompted a landslide of national recognition.

00:04:56.565 --> 00:04:59.484
- A game-changer in every sense for the Tigers.

00:05:01.059 --> 00:05:04.187
- It was a really close game, as well. We lost by one point, and that

00:05:04.177 --> 00:05:07.966
was the first time we've lost by that little in years.

00:05:08.247 --> 00:05:13.002
So everyone's already excited about that. The following Monday was insane.

00:05:13.077 --> 00:05:15.955
Like, everyone's just coming up to us and congratulating us.

00:05:16.554 --> 00:05:21.768
My phone is blowing up with messages and stuff from people that I don't even know.

00:05:22.412 --> 00:05:27.167
That really pushed me cuz I saw, like, people are noticing what I'm doing.

00:05:27.649 --> 00:05:31.778
So I have to play not only for myself but for my team.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.024
Cuz they're counting on me as well. 

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.776
- Alex made high school football history.

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:40.379
But let's be real: Nobody tries to go viral.

00:05:40.722 --> 00:05:43.082
Sometimes you just make history because you're you

00:05:43.929 --> 00:05:48.559
- I never saw it as a big deal. I see so many quarterbacks on this island

00:05:48.558 --> 00:05:52.386
doing that over and over and over and over, and I just feel bad because

00:05:52.634 --> 00:05:56.346
they're putting in the work. My boys are putting in the work on my team, and

00:05:56.726 --> 00:06:00.105
they are not getting all of this attention as well.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.054
All of the pressure does get to me sometimes.

00:06:05.012 --> 00:06:08.724
I'd say I had a lot more challenges this year than last year.

00:06:09.824 --> 00:06:13.036
Not only is it my second year playing for the varsity level, but

00:06:13.032 --> 00:06:16.892
I'm also getting all of this attention. People notice me now.

00:06:17.104 --> 00:06:20.483
- She's been struggling since our first game.

00:06:21.592 --> 00:06:27.181
- Things have gotten tough. And I know it hasn't been easy for them. 

00:06:27.522 --> 00:06:31.359
- She's thrown a number of picks, returned for, uh, touchdowns the other way.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:35.940
Anytime you're not doing well, you know, it's interesting

00:06:35.933 --> 00:06:37.767
how people will jump off the bandwagon.

00:06:38.727 --> 00:06:42.439
- Yeah, there's a lot of talking, but you just let that go through. You just focus on us. 

00:06:42.809 --> 00:06:47.897
- If someone's, like, hating on me or whatever, saying, like, "You don't deserve this.

00:06:47.893 --> 00:06:53.459
You don't deserve that attention and stuff," I sort of agree with them, so

00:06:53.456 --> 00:06:56.004
I don't really take it to heart, which helps, you know?

00:06:57.021 --> 00:06:57.730
Yeah.

00:07:00.598 --> 00:07:03.393
- I figure Alex and the team could use some home-field advantage.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.846
Since the L.A. Clippers were in town, I asked Tobias Harris and one of the only

00:07:10.837 --> 00:07:15.508
