00:08:50.345 --> 00:08:56.100
One of the guys read it early. He caught up to me and just sacked me.

00:08:57.788 --> 00:08:59.248
There was nothing I could do about it.

00:09:00.933 --> 00:09:05.854
I got up, and I thought I was fine. My coach goes to touch

00:09:05.853 --> 00:09:09.956
me, like, "Good job," and I flinched, like really badly.

00:09:11.728 --> 00:09:14.856
And he's like, "Oh. Does your shoulder hurt?" And I was like, "Yeah."

00:09:16.742 --> 00:09:19.995
I was out for the rest of the game. I couldn't do anything to help them.

00:09:22.312 --> 00:09:27.317
I felt bad because I felt like I let them down. They were counting on me.

00:09:28.817 --> 00:09:31.153
I'm the starting quarterback. I should be there.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:34.638
Like, I'm the one getting all these reps and working on these plays 

00:09:34.631 --> 00:09:38.122
just so I can help them do their jobs.

00:09:40.022 --> 00:09:44.777
In that moment especially, I felt like I let them down. And it was hard for me.

00:09:47.579 --> 00:09:48.997
I let my boys down.

00:09:54.805 --> 00:09:59.601
- Broken clavicle. So we're going to the hospital after this, but she wants

00:09:59.592 --> 00:10:03.096
to watch the rest of the game. That's how she is.

00:10:10.536 --> 00:10:12.455
